      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Expressed as an integer, $(-4)÷(\\frac{2}{5})\\times 6=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe multiply and divide, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)÷\\frac{2}{5}\\times 6 & = \\\\ ((-4)÷\\frac{2}{5})\\times 6 & = \\\\ (\\frac{-4}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{2})\\times 6 & = \\\\ (\\frac{(-4)\\times 5}{1\\times 2})\\times 6 & = \\\\ (-\\frac{20}{2})\\times 6 & = \\\\ (-10)\\times 6 & = \\\\ -60\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
